  "question": {
    "text": "Oxidation state of sulphur in anions $\\mathrm{SO}_3^{2-}, \\mathrm{S}_2 \\mathrm{O}_4^{2-}$ and $\\mathrm{S}_2 \\mathrm{O}_6^{2-}$ increases in the orders :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "x15s1",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{S}_2 \\mathrm{O}_6^{2-} < \\mathrm{S}_2 \\mathrm{O}_4^{2-} < \\mathrm{SO}_3^{2-}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ih05k",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{SO}_6^{2-} < \\mathrm{S}_2 \\mathrm{O}_4^{2-} < \\mathrm{S}_2 \\mathrm{O}_6^{2-}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9UxxG",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{S}_2 \\mathrm{O}_4^{2-} < \\mathrm{SO}_3^{2-} < \\mathrm{S}_2 \\mathrm{O}_6^{2-}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "bp2cT",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{S}_2 \\mathrm{O}_4^{2-} < \\mathrm{S}_2 \\mathrm{O}_6^{2-} < \\mathrm{SO}_3^{2-}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{In} \\mathrm{SO}_3^{--}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& x+3(-2)=-2 ; x=+4 \\\\\n& \\text { In } \\mathrm{S}_2 \\mathrm{O}_4^{--} \\\\\n& 2 x+4(-2)=-2 \\\\\n& 2 x-8=-2 \\\\\n& 2 x=6 ; \\quad x=+3 \\\\\n& \\text { In } \\mathrm{S}_2 \\mathrm{O}_6^{2-} \\\\\n& 2 x+6(-2)=-2 \\\\\n& 2 x=10 ; \\quad x=+5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nhence the correct order is\n$$\n\\mathrm{S}_2 \\mathrm{O}_4{ }^{--} < \\mathrm{SO}_3^{--} < \\mathrm{S}_2 \\mathrm{O}_6{ }^{--}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
